  "description": "Takes consistent, point-in-time file snapshots of a live SQLite database on a schedule using SQLite's Online Backup API (never an unsafe file copy), keeps the newest N, and writes them to a directory (or a pluggable store for object storage). A companion to streaming replication: use it when you want simple periodic full backups without an external binary or object-storage sidecar, or alongside `Rask.SQLite.Litestream` for a second line of defence. Register with `services.AddRaskSqliteSnapshots(...)`, or inject `ISqliteSnapshotter` to snapshot on demand. Standalone: depends only on Microsoft.Data.Sqlite and the Microsoft.Extensions hosting/DI abstractions.",
  "iconFile": "rask-icon.png",
